    ],
    "interpretation": "The 70B CF rate (5-7%) is 2-3x higher than 8B ZS (2.57%) and 20-30x higher than 8B FT (0.2-0.3%). Primary causes: (1) Zero-shot setting — fine-tuning teaches schema compliance, drastically reducing CF; (2) INT4 quantization likely contributes — reduced precision may degrade type consistency for entity mentions appearing in multiple relations; (3) Not a pure scale effect — 8B ZS Llama also shows high CF (1357 entities), suggesting the ZS→FT gap is the dominant factor."
